# Fly deploy (The Daily Tailor)

Production is `https://the-daily-tailor.fly.dev`. Code on `origin/main` is not live until Fly is deployed.

## One-time (if `FLY_API_TOKEN` is missing)

On Mac, remind Alessandro at session start (first message) and run or point to:

```bash
./deploy/fly/bootstrap-cloud-token.sh
```

That creates the deploy token and sets the GitHub Actions secret. He must still paste the printed token into the Cursor Cloud Agent environment secret `FLY_API_TOKEN`.

## After the token exists

- Push/land on `main` → GitHub Actions `.github/workflows/fly-deploy.yml` deploys.
- Cloud Agent / any VM with the secret: `./deploy/fly/deploy.sh` (no Mac).
- Do not tell Alessandro to deploy on the Mac if `FLY_API_TOKEN` is available here — run deploy yourself.
- After a fix that must hit the iPhone PWA, verify production (`/sw.js` cache version, or that `/api/morning-warm` does not hang past the server budget) before closing.

## Do not

- Leave production on a stale Fly image while claiming the bug is fixed on `main`.
- Commit tokens or `.env.local`.
